WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.050
Why does the first morning need code?

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.700
The pipeline sends a new hire's
account early, and disabled.

3
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.110
On the first morning, that person
needs an enabled account, a license,

4
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.362
baseline access, and a way to sign
in before their PIV card is bound.

5
00:00:14.362 --> 00:00:16.863
Lifecycle Workflows can do all of that.

6
00:00:16.863 --> 00:00:18.175
But here's the catch.

7
00:00:18.175 --> 00:00:21.838
Each workflow is a definition that
someone can change in the portal.

8
00:00:21.838 --> 00:00:26.525
And Learn makes every change a new
version, rather than an in-place update.

9
00:00:26.525 --> 00:00:30.200
So in this module you keep the
workflows as reviewed files.

10
00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.450
You lint them before
they reach the tenant.

11
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:35.475
You plan each change against
what the tenant holds.

12
00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:39.374
And then you measure how many hires
were actually ready on day one,

13
00:00:39.374 --> 00:00:43.250
because a workflow that ran isn't
the same as a person who can work.
